menu "Lab 6 (MQTT/TLS)"

    config LAB6_PLAINTEXT
        bool "Use plain MQTT (no TLS) instead of MQTT over TLS"
        default n
        help
            Default (n): connect with MQTT over TLS to mqtts://<LAB6_BROKER_HOST>:8883 and
            verify the broker against the CA cert embedded from
            main/certs/ca.crt (run broker/run_broker.sh first). This is the real
            lab target.

            When set (y): connect with plain MQTT to mqtt://<LAB6_BROKER_HOST>:1883 with no
            certificate. Provided for the automated QEMU smoke test only; the
            graded lab is the TLS path.

    config LAB6_BROKER_HOST
        string "Broker IP address, as the device sees it"
        default "10.0.2.2"
        help
            The app connects to mqtts://<this address>:8883 (or
            mqtt://<this address>:1883 with LAB6_PLAINTEXT). The default
            10.0.2.2 is this computer as seen from QEMU's user-mode
            network. On a board over Wi-Fi, set this computer's LAN IP
            address instead, and regenerate the certificates with it
            (bash ../broker/gen_certs.sh <LAN IP>): the broker certificate
            must list exactly this address in its subjectAltName.

endmenu
